\title{\bfseries Pseudo-Calabi--Yau Geometry on the Smooth Locus\\[0.2em]
\bfseries of the Announced Complex Six-Sphere\\[0.35em]
\large A null period curve and the semi-flat split-$G_2$ correspondence}
\author{}
\date{24 August 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
Assume Alp\"oge's announced construction~\cite{Alpoge} of a compact complex threefold $X$ diffeomorphic to $S^6$, fibred over $\PP^1$ by complex two-tori away from three special fibres.  We show that the smooth torus-fibred locus $X^\circ$ carries a natural semi-flat torsion-free $SU(1,2)$ structure, and therefore a Ricci-flat pseudo-K\"ahler metric of real signature $(2,4)$.

The construction is controlled by the fibrewise intersection form on $H^2(\TT^4,\RR)\cong\RR^{3,3}$.  Alp\"oge's monodromy fixes a primitive class
\[
  \eta=u\wedge w+6\gamma\wedge\delta
\]
of fibrewise type $(1,1)$ and signature $(1,1)$.  The meromorphic canonical form with divisor $2S_2-W$ restricts to a nowhere-vanishing holomorphic three-form $\Xi$ on $X^\circ$ and determines a holomorphic period one-form $\alpha=A(z)\,\dd z$.  If $\Omega=\sigma_1\wedge\sigma_2$ generates the fibrewise $(2,0)$ line, then
\[
 q(\eta,\eta)=12,\qquad q(\eta,\Omega)=0,\qquad
 q(\Omega,\Omega)=0,\qquad
 q(\Omega,\overline\Omega)=4\,\im\tau\,D,
\]
where $D=\im\beta-6(\im\mu)^2/\im\tau<0$.  These identities yield an explicit closed form
\[
 \omega=\frac{1}{\sqrt6}\eta-f^*\!\left(\frac{1}{8\ii}q(\alpha,\overline\alpha)\right)
\]
with $(\omega,\Xi)$ normalized as an $SU(1,2)$ structure.

The same data admit a period-domain interpretation.  A primitive of $\alpha$ is a holomorphic null curve in $\eta^\perp_\CC$, and its real part, together with the $\eta$ direction, defines a linearly full minimal immersion of signature $(1,2)$ into $\RR^{3,3}$.  Baraglia's split semi-flat correspondence reproduces the cylindrical torsion-free split-$G_2$ structure on $X^\circ\times S^1$.  The sign of $D$ simultaneously determines the signature of the Hodge three-plane and the real determinant of the torus period lattice, so $D=0$ is the common degeneration wall.  Finally, neither the pseudo-Calabi--Yau structure nor its cylindrical split-$G_2$ li